  "body": "### Summary\n\nWanted by LOT-048 (#74): only reply, edit and delete are captured or being captured (#264, #265); the answer to a **new topic** in a forum category (confirmation sentence and refresh target, E14) is still pending, so a new topic would be reported 'unconfirmed'.\n\n**Not authorised to post.** Creating a topic is a public write: it needs an explicit operator go (and a throwaway category/topic plan) before anything is sent.\n\n### Scope\n\nState to capture: the HFR answer page after posting a new topic in a forum category (sentence, refresh target, hidden fields of the new-topic form), anonymized.\n\n### Sources\n\n- LOT-048 spec and HFR-PROTOCOL write table (E14: pending)\n- #264 / PR #258 for the public-write capture method\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Operator go recorded on the PR before any post.\n- [ ] Anonymized capture and (if a parser consumes it) oracle output committed; row removed from the Capture backlog.\n- [ ] HFR-PROTOCOL write table E14 updated from the capture.\n\nRules: LOT-001 kit (`tooling/fixtures/`), anonymize every free-text field, independent leak check before any push, never hand-build the state in the cloud (LESSONS 36), legacy oracle when a parser consumes it, one PR per batch of captures, the PR removes the row from the Capture backlog in `docs/LOTS.md`. Write captures need the operator approval first.",
